  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warmer weather returns Wednesday along with breezy \nconditions and scattered showers. \n\nSurface high pressure will cross the eastern Great Lakes region \nthrough tonight. A southerly wind will increase on the backside of \nthe departing high and allow milder weather across most of the \nregion overnight. Low temperatures in the low to mid 40s are \nexpected. The surface high will still have a hold on the North \nCountry tonight, and temperatures are expected to reach the 30s \nacross the Tug Hill region/Lewis county. Patchy to areas of frost \nare possible. \n\nThe pressure gradient will tighten as a cold front approaches the \nregion Wednesday. Warm air advection within a 40knot low level jet \nwill spread across the forecast area. A southwest flow to about 3k \nfeet during peak heating will result in breezy conditions across the \nregion, especially northeast of Lake Erie. Wind gusts up to 38 mph \ncan't be ruled out across the Niagara Frontier Wednesday afternoon. \nIncreasing moisture ahead of a shortwave trough and cold front will \nsupport widely scattered showers across the region Wednesday \nafternoon. The cold front will cross the region Wednesday night.\nWinds will diminish quickly while shifting to the west \novernight. Showers are likely as the cold front crosses the \nregion. Rainfall amounts will be widely scattered and less than \n0.15\". \n\nA larger scale trough will move into the eastern Great Lakes region \nThursday through Friday. Seasonal temperatures with highs in the low \nto mid 60s are expected. A cool, westerly flow across the Lakes\nwill support lake effect and diurnal showers with most of the \nfocus across north-central NY Thursday.",
